IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-definitions-law`

-- Israel: the defined terms of s 1 of the Interpretation Ordinance [New Version], as functions that say what falls within each term.
--
-- s 1 lists 66 entries. Five read "(בוטלה)" (repealed) and carry only a note saying that the Law's definition governs earlier
-- enactments too (sin, misdemeanour, felony, coastal waters, fiscal year); the other 61 are here, except "year and month",
-- whose Gregorian calendar is chosen by il-interpretation-law.l4 and named again here. The conventions are those of
-- il-interpretation-definitions-law.l4:
--   * "includes" (לרבות) extends the ordinary meaning, so the ordinary meaning is a plain input (a judgement);
--   * a plain dash is exhaustive, so there is no such input;
--   * an entry that points at another entry calls that entry's function;
--   * FALSE always means "the thing is not within the term".
-- Where an entry's proviso says that in an earlier enactment the word has the meaning it would have had without the
-- Ordinance, the Ordinance's own notes sometimes state that earlier meaning and sometimes do not. Where a note states it, the
-- earlier meaning is a second function; where nothing states it, the answer is a named refusal. The notes are Wikisource's
-- editorial notes, not operative text, and NOTES.md says so.
-- The Ordinance's definitions govern the words of an enactment given before the Law (the head note and Law s 1); the
-- dispatcher at the end of this module says which entry governs which enactment.
-- Source: the unofficial Wikisource consolidation, ../../source/ordinance.wiki (src:ordinance:N). English glosses are mine; the Hebrew governs.

§ `Interpretation Ordinance s 1: the defined terms`

§§ `Nouns`

-- Entry "person" (אדם).
DECLARE `A candidate person` HAS
    `a person in the ordinary sense`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a company, association or body of persons`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `incorporated`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a company`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `an association`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a body of persons`                                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entries "ship" (אניה, ספינה) and "vessel" (כלי שיט).
DECLARE `A navigable thing` HAS
    `used for navigation`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `propelled by oars or paddles only`                                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A floating thing` HAS
    `its facts as a ship`                                              IS A `A navigable thing`
    `a boat`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a raft`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `any other thing made to float`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "representative of the Attorney General" (בא כוח, או נציג, של היועץ המשפטי לממשלה).
DECLARE `A post under the Attorney General` IS ONE OF
    `the State Attorney`
    `a deputy or assistant of the State Attorney`
    `the deputy of the State Attorney`
    `an assistant of the State Attorney`
    `a district attorney or a deputy district attorney`
    `a district attorney`
    `a deputy of a district attorney`
    `a county attorney`
    `a person whom the Attorney General authorised to be his representative or agent`
    `anyone else`

-- Entry "repeal" (ביטול).
DECLARE `A way a law ceased to be valid` IS ONE OF
    `repeal of the law as a whole`
    `repeal of part of the law`
    `a provision by or under which the law or a part of it ceased to be valid`
    `a repeal in its ordinary sense of a kind the entry does not list`
    `something that is not a repeal in its ordinary sense`
    `anything else`

-- Entry "house" (בית).
DECLARE `A building or place` HAS
