-- The words whose entries carry a proviso ("where the word appears in an enactment given before ..., its meaning is as it would
-- have been but for ..."), the dates the provisos turn on, and which meaning governs. The sources give none of those dates
-- (the Ordinance's commencement section is repealed, and the Movables Law and the Land Law are not among the sources;
-- the signature line gives only the Minister's date, 1954-01-01, which is not the date the new text was published), so each
-- is a plain fact the caller supplies.
DECLARE `A word with an earlier meaning` IS ONE OF
    `the word statute`
    `the word enactment`
    `the word ordinance`
    `the word regulation`
    `the word movables`
    `the word immovables`

DECLARE `The age of the enactment a word stands in` HAS
    `given before the new text of the Ordinance was published`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `given before the Ordinance began to have effect`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `given before the Movables Law, 5731-1971, began to have effect`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `given before the Land Law, 5729-1969, began to have effect`        IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Which meaning of a word governs` IS ONE OF
    `the definition the Ordinance now states`
    `the earlier meaning that the Ordinance's note states`
    `the earlier meaning, which this text does not state`

-- The entries, one constructor each, for the dispatcher at the end.

§§ `Entries about persons, offices and bodies`

-- src:ordinance:33 | ”אדם“ – לרבות חברה או התאחדות או חבר בני אדם, בין שהם מואגדים ובין שאינם מואגדים;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "person" (src:ordinance:33)
-- "Includes a company, association or body of persons, whether incorporated or not": the extension does not turn on
-- incorporation, so `incorporated` is read by nothing and tests show that it changes no answer.
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "person" — the candidate is a person:` c MEANS
       c's `a person in the ordinary sense`
    OR c's `a company, association or body of persons`
    OR c's `a company`
    OR c's `an association`
    OR c's `a body of persons`

-- src:ordinance:35 | ”בא כוח, או נציג, של היועץ המשפטי לממשלה“ – פרקליט המדינה, משנהו או סגניו, פרקליטי מחוז או סגניהם, פרקליטי נפה וכל מי שהיועץ המשפטי הסמיכו להיות בא כוחו או נציגו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "representative of the Attorney General" (src:ordinance:35)
GIVEN post IS A `A post under the Attorney General`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "representative of the Attorney General" — the post is one:` post MEANS
    CONSIDER post
    WHEN `the State Attorney`                                                                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a deputy or assistant of the State Attorney`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the deputy of the State Attorney`                                                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an assistant of the State Attorney`                                                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a district attorney or a deputy district attorney`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a district attorney`                                                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a deputy of a district attorney`                                                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a county attorney`                                                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person whom the Attorney General authorised to be his representative or agent`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else`                                                                               THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:38 | ”בית משפט“ – כל בית משפט בן־סמך לשפוט בישראל;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "court" (src:ordinance:38)
GIVEN t IS A `A tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "court" — the tribunal is a court:` t MEANS
        t's `a court`
    AND t's `competent to adjudicate in Israel`

-- src:ordinance:39 | ”בית משפט לערעורים אזרחיים“ – בית המשפט העליון כשהוא יושב כבית משפט לערעורים אזרחיים;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "court of civil appeals" (src:ordinance:39)
GIVEN s IS A `A sitting of a court`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "court of civil appeals" — the sitting is one:` s MEANS
        s's `the Supreme Court`
    AND CONSIDER s's `the capacity in which it sits`
        WHEN `as a court of civil appeals`    THEN TRUE
        WHEN `as a court of criminal appeals` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `in some other capacity`         THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:40 | ”בית משפט לערעורים פליליים“ – בית המשפט העליון כשהוא יושב בדין כבית משפט לערעורים פליליים;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "court of criminal appeals" (src:ordinance:40)
GIVEN s IS A `A sitting of a court`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "court of criminal appeals" — the sitting is one:` s MEANS
        s's `the Supreme Court`
    AND CONSIDER s's `the capacity in which it sits`
        WHEN `as a court of civil appeals`    THEN FALSE
        WHEN `as a court of criminal appeals` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `in some other capacity`         THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:47 | ”הצהרה בשבועה“ – לרבות מסמך שבאו עליו הן־צדק או הצהרה מפי אדם שהותרו לו, על פי דין, הן־צדק או הצהרה במקום שבועה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "declaration on oath" (src:ordinance:47)
GIVEN x IS A `A sworn or affirmed statement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "declaration on oath" — the statement is one:` x MEANS
       x's `a declaration on oath or an oath in the ordinary sense`
    OR x's `a document bearing an affirmation`
    OR x's `a declaration by a person whom a law permits an affirmation or declaration in place of an oath`

-- src:ordinance:102 | ”שבועה“ – לרבות הן־צדק והצהרה מפי אדם שהותרו לו, על פי דין, הן־צדק או הצהרה במקום שבועה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "oath" (src:ordinance:102)
GIVEN x IS A `A sworn or affirmed statement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "oath" — the statement is an oath:` x MEANS
       x's `a declaration on oath or an oath in the ordinary sense`
    OR x's `an affirmation`
    OR x's `a declaration by a person whom a law permits an affirmation or declaration in place of an oath`

-- src:ordinance:53 | ”חתימה“, באדם שאינו יכול לכתוב שמו – לרבות ”סימן“;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "signature" (src:ordinance:53)
GIVEN s IS A `A signature`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "signature" — the signature counts:` s MEANS
       s's `a signature in the ordinary sense`
    OR (s's `by a person who cannot write his name` AND s's `a mark`)

-- src:ordinance:61 | ”מדפיס ממשלתי“ – המדפיס הממשלתי של ישראל, ולענין חיקוק או לענין מסמך של המדינה – אף כל מדפיס אחר שהממשלה הרשתה אותו, דרך כלל או במיוחד, להדפיס אותו חיקוק או מסמך, וכל חיקוק או מסמך כאמור הנחזה כנדפס על ידי המדפיס הממשלתי או על ידי מדפיס אחר שהורשה לכך כאמור, יראוהו כאילו נדפס כך אם לא הוכח היפוכו של דבר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Government Printer" (src:ordinance:61)
-- The Government Printer of Israel; and, for an enactment or State document, any other printer the Government has authorised.
GIVEN p IS A `A printer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Government Printer" — the printer is the Government Printer:` p MEANS
       p's `the Government Printer of Israel`
    OR (    p's `the thing printed is an enactment or a State document`
        AND p's `the Government authorised it, generally or specially, to print that enactment or document`)

-- The presumption in the same entry: an enactment or document that purports to be printed by the Government Printer, or by
-- another printer so authorised, is treated as so printed "if the contrary is not proved". FALSE means the presumption does not apply.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Government Printer" (the presumption) (src:ordinance:61)
GIVEN d IS A `A printed enactment or document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Government Printer" — the enactment or document is treated as printed by the Government Printer or an authorised printer:` d MEANS
        d's `it purports to be printed by the Government Printer or by another printer so authorised`
    AND NOT d's `the contrary has been proved`

-- src:ordinance:62 | ”מזכיר הממשלה“ – הפקיד שנתמנה על ידי הממשלה להיות מזכיר הממשלה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Secretary to the Government" (src:ordinance:62)
GIVEN o IS AN `An official`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Secretary to the Government" — the official is the Secretary to the Government:` o MEANS
    o's `appointed by the Government to be Secretary to the Government`

-- src:ordinance:74 | ”מפקח כללי של המשטרה“ – לרבות סגן המפקח הכללי של המשטרה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Inspector General of Police" (src:ordinance:74)
GIVEN h IS A `A holder of the police post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Inspector General of Police" — the holder is within the term:` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `the Inspector General of Police`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Deputy Inspector General of Police`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else`                                THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:77 | ”נציב בתי הסוהר“ – לרבות סגן נציב בתי הסוהר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Commissioner of Prisons" (src:ordinance:77)
GIVEN h IS A `A holder of the prisons post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Commissioner of Prisons" — the holder is within the term:` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `the Commissioner of Prisons`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Deputy Commissioner of Prisons`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else`                            THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:81 | ”עובד ציבורי“ או ”משרד ציבורי“ – לרבות כל עובד או משרד שהוטלו עליהם תפקידים בעלי אופי רשמי, או הממלאים תפקידים כאלה, בין שהם נתונים לפיקוחה הישיר של ממשלה ובין אם לאו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "public servant" (src:ordinance:81)
-- "Includes any employee or office on whom duties of an official character are imposed, or who fills such duties, whether or
-- not under the direct supervision of a government": supervision does not change the answer and is read by nothing.
GIVEN w IS A `A worker or office`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "public servant" — the worker or office is a public servant or public office:` w MEANS
       w's `a public servant or public office in the ordinary sense`
    OR w's `duties of an official character are imposed on it`
    OR w's `it fills duties of that character`

-- src:ordinance:97 | ”רופא ממשלתי“ – רופא בשירות המדינה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Government doctor" (src:ordinance:97)
GIVEN x IS A `A doctor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Government doctor" — the doctor is a Government doctor:` x MEANS
        x's `a doctor`
    AND x's `in the service of the State`

-- src:ordinance:98 | ”רופא מוסמך“ – אדם הרשום בישראל כרופא לפי הדין הנוהג אותה שעה בענין רישום רופאים;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "qualified doctor" (src:ordinance:98)
GIVEN x IS A `A doctor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "qualified doctor" — the person is a qualified doctor:` x MEANS
        x's `registered in Israel as a doctor`
    AND x's `registered under the law in force at that time on the registration of doctors`

-- src:ordinance:101 | ”רשות מקומית“ – עיריה, מועצה מקומית או רשות כיוצא באלה, שנתכוננו בכוח חוק בר־תוקף אותה שעה, הקובע הוראות בדבר הקמת רשויות של שלטון מקומי;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "local authority" (src:ordinance:101)
GIVEN b IS A `A local body under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "local authority" — the body is a local authority:` b MEANS
       (   b's `a municipality, a local council or an authority like them`
        OR b's `a municipality`
        OR b's `a local council`
        OR b's `an authority like them`)
    AND b's `constituted by a law in force at that time`
    AND b's `that law provides for the establishment of local-government authorities`

-- src:ordinance:95 | ”קונסול“ או ”נציג קונסולרי“ – קונסול כללי, קונסול, סגן קונסול וכל המוסמך אותה שעה למלא תפקידו של אחד מאלה, וכן סוכן קונסולרי;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "consul" (src:ordinance:95)
-- The same list as s 3 of the Law ("authorised at that time" is the Law's "authorised to fill"), so this calls the Law's function.
GIVEN post IS A `A consular post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "consul" — the post is one:` post MEANS
    `s 3 "consul" — the post is one:` post

-- src:ordinance:103 | ”שוטר“ – כל הנמנה עם חיל המשטרה; ו”קצין משטרה גבוה“ – כל קצין משטרה בדרגת עוזר מפקד מחוז ומעלה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "policeman" (src:ordinance:103)
GIVEN x IS A `A police officer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "policeman" — the person is a policeman:` x MEANS
    x's `a member of the police force`

-- The second term of the same entry: a senior police officer is any police officer of the rank of assistant district
-- commander and above.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "policeman" (second term: senior police officer) (src:ordinance:103)
GIVEN x IS A `A police officer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "policeman" — the officer is a senior police officer:` x MEANS
        x's `a member of the police force`
    AND x's `of the rank of assistant district commander or higher`

-- src:ordinance:104 | ”שופט“, לענין שופטי בית המשפט העליון – אף נשיא בית המשפט העליון במשמע; ולענין שופטי בתי המשפט המחוזיים – אף הנשיאים וסגני הנשיאים במשמע;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "judge" (src:ordinance:104)
-- "Judge", for the judges of the Supreme Court, includes the President of the Supreme Court; for judges of the district
-- courts, includes the presidents and vice-presidents. For any other court the entry says nothing, and a judge of that
-- court is a judge in the ordinary sense (the word is then what it ordinarily is). The office of president of a magistrates' court is not
-- one the entry extends the word to, so it is outside the extension (FALSE); a president who is also a judge of that court is `a judge of another court`.
GIVEN refersTo IS A `What the word judge refers to`
      office IS A `A judicial office`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "judge" — the word refers to` refersTo `, and the office is` office MEANS
    CONSIDER refersTo
    WHEN `judges of the Supreme Court` THEN
        CONSIDER office
        WHEN `a judge of the Supreme Court`                THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the President of the Supreme Court`          THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `judges of the district courts` THEN
        CONSIDER office
        WHEN `a judge of a district court`                 THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a president of a district court`             THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a vice-president of a district court`        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `judges of another court` THEN
        CONSIDER office
        WHEN `a judge of another court`                    THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:ordinance:105 | ”שופט של בית משפט שלום“ – מי שבידו כתב מינוי להיות שופט של בית משפט שלום;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "magistrates' court judge" (src:ordinance:105)
GIVEN x IS A `A person with an appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "magistrates' court judge" — the person is one:` x MEANS
    x's `holds a letter of appointment as judge of a magistrates' court`

§§ `Entries about things, places and craft`

-- src:ordinance:34 | ”אניה“ או ”ספינה“ – כל כלי המשמש בשיט ואינו מונע במשוטים או במשוטי־דחף בלבד;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "ship" (src:ordinance:34)
GIVEN t IS A `A navigable thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "ship" — the thing is a ship:` t MEANS
        t's `used for navigation`
    AND NOT t's `propelled by oars or paddles only`

-- src:ordinance:59 | ”כלי שיט“ – אניה, ספינה, סירה, אסדה וכל כלי אחר העשוי לשוט;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "vessel" (src:ordinance:59)
GIVEN t IS A `A floating thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "vessel" — the thing is a vessel:` t MEANS
       `Ordinance s 1 "ship" — the thing is a ship:` (t's `its facts as a ship`)
    OR t's `a boat`
    OR t's `a raft`
    OR t's `any other thing made to float`

-- src:ordinance:58 | ”כלי טיס“ – כל מכונת טיס, דאון, ספינת־אויר או כדור פורח, בין מחובר ובין שאינו מחובר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "aircraft" (src:ordinance:58)
GIVEN t IS A `A flying thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "aircraft" — the thing is an aircraft:` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a flying machine`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a glider`                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an airship`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a balloon, tethered or not`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anything else`                  THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:73 | ”מפקד“, בכלי טיס – מי שבידו אותה שעה השליטה על כלי טיס או מי שממונה עליו אותה שעה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "commander of an aircraft" (src:ordinance:73)
GIVEN x IS A `A person in relation to an aircraft`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "commander of an aircraft" — the person is the commander:` x MEANS
       x's `has control of the aircraft at that time`
    OR x's `is appointed over the one who has control at that time`

-- src:ordinance:96 | ”קברניט“ – מי שבידו השליטה על ספינה או על אניה, או מי שממונה עליה אותה שעה להוציא נווט ורב חובל־נמל;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "master" (src:ordinance:96)
-- "Whoever has control of a ship or vessel, or whoever is appointed over it at that time, except a navigator and a harbour
-- master" (the Hebrew "להוציא" is "excluding"). READING TAKEN (fork F32): the exclusion closes the whole sentence, so it
-- reaches the first limb as well; a navigator or harbour master who has control is not the master.
GIVEN x IS A `A person in relation to a ship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "master" — the person is the master:` x MEANS
        (x's `has control of a ship or vessel` OR x's `is appointed over the ship or vessel at that time`)
    AND NOT x's `a navigator`
    AND NOT x's `a harbour master`

-- The other reading (F32): the exclusion belongs to the second limb only.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "master" (the exclusion belongs to the second limb only) (src:ordinance:96)
GIVEN x IS A `A person in relation to a ship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "master" — the person is the master, if the exclusion belongs to the second limb only:` x MEANS
       x's `has control of a ship or vessel`
    OR (    x's `is appointed over the ship or vessel at that time`
        AND NOT x's `a navigator`
        AND NOT x's `a harbour master`)

-- src:ordinance:54 | ”ייבוא“ – הבאה או גרם הבאה לישראל, בים, ביבשה או באויר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "import" (src:ordinance:54)
GIVEN m IS A `A movement across Israel's border`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "import" — the movement is an import:` m MEANS
        m's `into Israel`
    AND m's `done, or caused to be done`
    AND (m's `by sea, land or air` OR m's `by sea` OR m's `by land` OR m's `by air`)

-- src:ordinance:56 | ”ייצוא“ – הוצאה או גרם הוצאה מישראל, בים, ביבשה או באויר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "export" (src:ordinance:56)
GIVEN m IS A `A movement across Israel's border`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "export" — the movement is an export:` m MEANS
        m's `out of Israel`
    AND m's `done, or caused to be done`
    AND (m's `by sea, land or air` OR m's `by sea` OR m's `by land` OR m's `by air`)

-- src:ordinance:55 | ”יורד ים“ – לרבות כל אדם העובד בספינה או המועסק בה בכל תפקיד שהוא, חוץ מקברניט ומנווט וחוץ מחניך הקשור בחוזה ורשום כראוי;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "seaman" (src:ordinance:55)
-- "Includes any person working on a ship or employed on it in any capacity, except the master and a navigator and except an
-- apprentice bound by a contract and properly registered." READING TAKEN: the exceptions limit what the word is extended to; they
-- do not remove from the word anyone who is a seaman in its ordinary sense.
GIVEN p IS A `A person aboard a ship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "seaman" — the person is a seaman:` p MEANS
       p's `a seaman in the ordinary sense`
    OR (    (   p's `works on a ship or is employed on it in any capacity`
             OR p's `works on a ship`
             OR p's `is employed on a ship in any capacity`)
        AND NOT p's `the master`
        AND NOT p's `a navigator`
        AND NOT p's `an apprentice bound by a contract and properly registered`)

-- src:ordinance:57 | ”ישראל“ או ”המדינה“ – לרבות מימי חופין שלה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Israel" (src:ordinance:57)
-- "Israel" or "the State" includes its coastal waters. The strip is the one s 3 of the Law gives (the Ordinance's own entry for
-- coastal waters is repealed and its note defers to the Law, F14, F29).
GIVEN p IS A `A place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Israel" — the place is Israel or the State:` p MEANS
       p's `in the territory of the State in the ordinary sense`
    OR CONSIDER p's `its position, if it is at sea`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST pt THEN `s 3 "coastal waters" — the point is within the coastal waters:` pt

-- src:ordinance:60 | ”לירה“ – לירה ישראלית;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "pound" (src:ordinance:60)
GIVEN p IS A `A pound`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "pound" — the pound is within the term:` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an Israeli pound`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a pound of another country`     THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:37 | ”בית“ – לרבות כל בית, חלק מבית, וכל בנין או מבנה אחר, שאנוש דר בהם או תופש אותם, בזכות עצמו או בדרך אחרת, אם ביום ואם בלילה, או שנועדו לדירה או לתפישה כגון זו, ובין שכולם מעל לפני הקרקע ובין שכולם או מקצתם מתחת לפני הקרקע;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "house" (src:ordinance:37)
-- Whether it lies above the ground or below it makes no difference ("whether wholly above the surface or wholly or partly
-- below"), so `wholly or partly below the surface of the ground` is read by nothing.
GIVEN b IS A `A building or place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "house" — the building or place is a house:` b MEANS
       b's `a house in the ordinary sense`
    OR b's `a part of a house`
    OR (    (b's `a building or other structure` OR b's `a building` OR b's `another structure`)
        AND (   b's `people dwell in it or occupy it, by right or otherwise, by day or night`
             OR b's `it was intended for dwelling or occupation`))

-- src:ordinance:99 | ”רחוב“ או ”דרך“ – לרבות כביש, שדרה, סמטה, משעול לרוכבים או לרגלים, ככר, חצר, טיילת, מבוי, מפלש וכל מקום פתוח שהציבור משתמש בו או נוהג לעבור בו, או שהציבור נכנס אליו או רשאי להיכנס אליו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "street" (src:ordinance:99)
-- "Includes a highway, avenue, lane, bridle path or footpath, square, courtyard, promenade, alley, passage, and any open
-- place that the public uses or customarily passes through, or that the public enters or may enter."
GIVEN w IS A `A way or place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "street" — the way or place is a street or road:` w MEANS
       w's `a street or road in the ordinary sense`
    OR w's `of one of the kinds listed`
    OR w's `a highway`
    OR w's `an avenue`
    OR w's `a lane`
    OR w's `a bridle path`
    OR w's `a footpath`
    OR w's `a square`
    OR w's `a courtyard`
    OR w's `a promenade`
    OR w's `an alley`
    OR w's `a passage`
    OR (    w's `an open place`
        AND (   w's `the public uses it or customarily passes through it`
             OR w's `the public enters it or may enter it`))

-- src:ordinance:64 | ”מחוז“ – אחד המחוזות המינהליים ששטח המדינה מחולק להם על פי חיקוק;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "district" (src:ordinance:64)
GIVEN x IS A `A division of the State's area under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "district" — the division is a district:` x MEANS
        x's `an administrative district`
    AND x's `the area of the State is divided into it by virtue of an enactment`

§§ `Entries about law, enactments, statutes and regulations (with the provisos that point at earlier meanings)`

-- The refusal for a proviso whose earlier meaning the sources do not state.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Ordinance states no earlier meaning of "enactment": its entry says only that the word means what it would have meant without the Ordinance` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Ordinance states no earlier meaning of enactment: its entry says only that the word means what it would have meant without the Ordinance, and no note or other text of the sources says what that was"

-- The refusal for an open ("includes") entry and a thing it does not list. The entry puts its listed members in, and keeps nothing out;
-- whether an unlisted thing is within the term depends on the word's ordinary meaning, which the Ordinance does not define.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing` MEANS
    REFUSE "the entry says what the term includes and says nothing that puts this unlisted thing in or out of it: whether it falls within the term depends on the ordinary meaning of the word, which the Ordinance does not define; say so by choosing the constructor for a thing that is within the ordinary meaning, or for one that is not"

-- The refusal for "determined" and a regulation that uses the word.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Ordinance's entry on "determined" says nothing of a regulation that itself uses the word` MEANS
    REFUSE "the entry on determined speaks of the law in which the word appears and of regulations made under that law; it says nothing of a regulation in which the word itself appears, so the sources do not say whether a determination made in that regulation, or in regulations made under it, counts"

-- src:ordinance:48 | ”חוק“ – דבר חקיקה של הכנסת ולרבות כל פקודה; אולם מקום שהמלה ”חוק“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני פרסום הנוסח החדש לפקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא הנוסח החדש;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "ordinance" (the current definition, which the entry "statute" includes) (src:ordinance:48)
-- The current text of the entry "ordinance" is quoted below under its own heading; "statute" includes every ordinance.
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate statute under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "statute" — the candidate is a statute, as the Ordinance now defines it:` c MEANS
       c's `a legislative act of the Knesset`
    OR `Ordinance s 1 "ordinance" — the candidate is an ordinance, as the Ordinance now defines it:` c

-- src:ordinance:87 | ”פקודה“ – כל פקודה שניתנה מאת מועצת המדינה הזמנית וכל פקודה שניתנה כדין בארץ ישראל לפני הקמת המדינה, ופקודה זו בכלל; אולם מקום שהמלה ”פקודה“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא פקודה זו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "ordinance" (src:ordinance:87)
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate statute under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "ordinance" — the candidate is an ordinance, as the Ordinance now defines it:` c MEANS
       c's `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State`
    OR c's `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established`
    OR c's `this Ordinance itself`

-- src:ordinance:49 | ההגדרה החלה על חיקוק שניתן לפני פרסום הנוסח החדש לפקודה זו היא ההגדרה ”דין“ בנוסח החדש לפקודה זו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "statute", the note (the earlier meaning is the entry "law") (src:ordinance:49)
GIVEN source IS A `A source that may be law under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "statute" — in an enactment given before the new text was published, the word means "law", and the source is one:` source MEANS
    `Ordinance s 1 "law" — the source is law:` source

-- src:ordinance:52 | ”חיקוק“ – כל חוק וכל תקנה בין שניתנו לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו ובין שניתנו לאחריה; אולם מקום שהמלה ”חיקוק“ באה בפקודה או בתקנה שניתנו לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא פקודה זו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "enactment" (src:ordinance:52)
GIVEN i IS AN `An instrument under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "enactment" — the instrument is an enactment, as the Ordinance now defines it:` i MEANS
       `Ordinance s 1 "statute" — the candidate is a statute, as the Ordinance now defines it:` (i's `taken as a statute`)
    OR `Ordinance s 1 "regulation" — the instrument is a regulation, as the Ordinance now defines it:` i

@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "enactment" (the proviso: no earlier meaning is stated) (src:ordinance:52)
GIVEN age IS AN `The age of the enactment a word stands in`
      i IS AN `An instrument under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "enactment" — the word standing in an enactment of the age` age `, the instrument is an enactment:` i MEANS
    CONSIDER `Ordinance s 1 — which meaning governs the word` `the word enactment` `in an enactment of the age` age
    WHEN `the definition the Ordinance now states` THEN
        `Ordinance s 1 "enactment" — the instrument is an enactment, as the Ordinance now defines it:` i
    OTHERWISE
        `the Ordinance states no earlier meaning of "enactment": its entry says only that the word means what it would have meant without the Ordinance`

-- src:ordinance:112 | ”תקנה“ – תקנה, כלל, חוק עזר, מנשר, אכרזה, צו, הוראה, הודעה, מודעה, או מסמך אחר, שניתנו מאת כל רשות בארץ ישראל או בישראל, בין לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו ובין לאחריה, מכוח חוק, או מכוח אקט של הפרלמנט הבריטי או מכוח דבר־המלך־במועצה, לרבות צו, הוראה, הודעה, מודעה או מסמך אחר שניתנו על יסוד תקנה, כלל או חוק עזר כאמור; אולם מקום שהמלה ”תקנה“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא פקודה זו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "regulation" (src:ordinance:112)
-- "A regulation, rule, by-law, proclamation, manifesto, order, direction, notice, announcement or other document given by any
-- authority in Palestine or in Israel, before or after the Ordinance, by virtue of a law, or of an Act of the British Parliament,
-- or of an Order in Council, including an order, direction, notice, announcement or other document given on the basis of such a
-- regulation, rule or by-law." The "law" the instrument was given by virtue of is asked of the entry "statute".
GIVEN i IS AN `An instrument under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "regulation" — the instrument is a regulation, as the Ordinance now defines it:` i MEANS
        (   i's `a regulation, rule, by-law, proclamation, manifesto, order, direction, notice, announcement or other document`
         OR i's `a regulation`
         OR i's `a rule`
         OR i's `a by-law`
         OR i's `a manifesto`
         OR i's `a proclamation`
         OR i's `an order`
         OR i's `a direction`
         OR i's `a notice`
         OR i's `an announcement`
         OR i's `another document`)
    AND (   (    i's `given by an authority in Palestine or in Israel`
             AND (`by virtue of a statute` OR i's `given by virtue of an Act of the British Parliament or an Order in Council`))
         OR i's `given on the basis of a regulation, rule or by-law of that kind`)
    WHERE
        `by virtue of a statute` MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `the statute it was given by virtue of`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `Ordinance s 1 "statute" — the candidate is a statute, as the Ordinance now defines it:` c

-- src:ordinance:113 | ההגדרה החלה על חיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו: ”תקנות“ – כוללות תקנות וחוקי עזר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "regulation", the note: the earlier meaning (src:ordinance:113)
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate for the earlier meaning of regulation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "regulation" — in an enactment given before the Ordinance took effect, the candidate is within the earlier meaning:` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a regulation`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a by-law`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not a regulation or by-law in its ordinary sense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else`    THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- src:ordinance:88 | ההגדרה החלה על חיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו: ”פקודה“ – פירושה כל חוק מטעם המוסד המחוקק של ישראל, לרבות צוויים מאת הנציב העליון במועצה, צווים מאת הנציב העליון (מקור ההגדרה הוא מתקופת המנדט הבריטי) ותקנות או צווים שהוצאו עפ״י איזו פקודה, ופקודה שיש לה שם קצר אפשר לקרוא לה לכל דבר בשמה הקצר;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "ordinance", the note: the earlier meaning (src:ordinance:88)
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate for the earlier meaning of ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "ordinance" — in an enactment given before the Ordinance took effect, the candidate is within the earlier meaning:` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a law of the legislative authority`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Order in Council`                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order of the High Commissioner in Council`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order of the High Commissioner`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulations or orders made under an ordinance`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulations made under an ordinance`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `orders made under an ordinance`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not an ordinance in the ordinary sense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else`                                     THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- The same note's last clause: "an ordinance that has a short name may be called by that name for all purposes". A reference
-- reaches the ordinance when the ordinance has a short name and the reference uses that name.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "ordinance", the note: the short name (src:ordinance:88)
GIVEN hasShort IS A BOOLEAN
      usesIt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "ordinance" — in an earlier enactment, the ordinance has a short name:` hasShort `, and the reference uses that short name:` usesIt `, so the reference reaches the ordinance` MEANS
    hasShort AND usesIt

-- src:ordinance:42 | ”דין“ – לרבות כל אחד מאלה:
-- src:ordinance:43 | (1) חיקוק;
-- src:ordinance:44 | (2) אקט של הפרלמנט הבריטי או חלק ממנו, ודבר־המלך־במועצה או חלק ממנו, בין שניתנו לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו ובין שניתנו לאחריה, וכפי תקפם בארץ ישראל לפני הקמת המדינה או כפי תקפם במדינה;
-- src:ordinance:45 | (3) צווים, תקנות, כללים, חוקי עזר, מנשרים, הוראות, הודעות וכל מסמך אחר, שניתנו מכוח ”דין“ כמשמעותו בפסקה (2) של הגדרה זו, בין לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו ובין לאחריה, ואינם בגדר חיקוקים, וכפי תקפם בארץ ישראל לפני הקמת המדינה או כפי תקפם במדינה;
-- src:ordinance:46 | (4) דינים עותומניים, דינים דתיים בין שבכתב ובין שבעל־פה, דיני המשפט המקובל ועקרוני היושר של אנגליה, כפי תקפם בארץ ישראל לפני הקמת המדינה או כפי תקפם במדינה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "law" (stem and limbs (1) to (4)) (src:ordinance:42-46)
-- "Includes" each of: (1) an enactment; (2) an Act of the British Parliament or part of it, an Order in Council or part of it,
-- as in force in Palestine before the State was established or as in force in the State; (3) orders, regulations, rules, by-laws,
-- proclamations, notices and other documents given by virtue of such an Act or Order, not being enactments, as so in force;
-- (4) Ottoman law, religious law written or oral, the common law and the principles of equity of England, as so in force.
-- Everything that is law in the ordinary sense stays law ("includes"). The entry is OPEN: a source it does not list is neither
-- put in nor kept out by the entry, so `any other source` refuses, and the caller settles it by choosing `anything that is law
-- in its ordinary sense` (an Israeli Supreme Court precedent is one) or `something that is not law in its ordinary sense`.
-- Each member of a list in the entry is a constructor of its own beside the phrase as printed (the Law's closed entry,
-- s 3 "law", answers FALSE for a source it does not list: `any other source` there is outside a list that says "each of these").
GIVEN source IS A `A source that may be law under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "law" — the source is law:` source MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `anything that is law in its ordinary sense`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not law in its ordinary sense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enactment` i                              THEN `Ordinance s 1 "enactment" — the instrument is an enactment, as the Ordinance now defines it:` i
    WHEN `an Act of the British Parliament or part of it, or an Order in Council or part of it` inForce
                                                       THEN inForce
    WHEN `an Act of the British Parliament or part of it` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `an Order in Council or part of it` inForce   THEN inForce
    WHEN `an order, regulation, rule, by-law, proclamation, notice or other document given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce
                                                       THEN inForce
    WHEN `an order given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `a regulation given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `a rule given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `a by-law given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `a manifesto given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `a direction given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `a notice given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `another document given by virtue of such an Act or Order, and not an enactment` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `Ottoman law` inForce                         THEN inForce
    WHEN `religious law, oral or written` inForce      THEN inForce
    WHEN `oral religious law` inForce                  THEN inForce
    WHEN `written religious law` inForce               THEN inForce
    WHEN `the common law and the principles of equity of England` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `the common law of England` inForce           THEN inForce
    WHEN `the principles of equity of England` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `any other source`                            THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- src:ordinance:36 | ”ביטול“, של דין – לרבות ביטולו של חלק ממנו, ולרבות הוראה שעל פיה או מכוחה חדל הדין או חלק ממנו להיות בר־תוקף;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "repeal" (src:ordinance:36)
-- "Includes" repeal of part of the law and a provision by which the law or a part of it ceases to be valid: an OPEN entry, so a
-- way the entry does not list is put in or out by the caller's choice of constructor, and `anything else` refuses.
GIVEN w IS A `A way a law ceased to be valid`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "repeal" — the way the law ceased to be valid is a repeal:` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `repeal of the law as a whole`                                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `repeal of part of the law`                                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision by or under which the law or a part of it ceased to be valid`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a repeal in its ordinary sense of a kind the entry does not list`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not a repeal in its ordinary sense`                              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else`                                                                     THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- src:ordinance:41 | ”בכתב“ – לרבות בדפוס, בליתוגרפיה, במכונת כתיבה, בצילום ובכל דרך אחרת של הצגת מלים או ספרות, או העתקתן, בצורה הנראית לעין;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "in writing" (src:ordinance:41)
-- "Includes print, lithography, typewriting, photography and every other way of presenting words or numerals, or copying them,
-- in a form visible to the eye." The four named ways are instances of presenting or copying words or numerals.
-- READING TAKEN: "in a form visible to the eye" governs the whole list.
GIVEN p IS A `A presentation of words or numerals`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "in writing" — the presentation counts as writing:` p MEANS
       p's `writing in the ordinary sense`
    OR (    (   p's `presents words or numerals, or copies them`
             OR p's `by printing`
             OR p's `by lithography`
             OR p's `by typewriting`
             OR p's `by photography`)
        AND p's `in a form visible to the eye`)

-- src:ordinance:63 | ”מודעה לרבים“ – הודעה של הממשלה, או מטעמה, שאינה בת־פעל תחיקתי ונתפרסמה ברשומות;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "public notice" (src:ordinance:63)
GIVEN n IS A `A notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "public notice" — the notice is a public notice:` n MEANS
        n's `of the Government or on its behalf`
    AND NOT n's `of legislative effect`
    AND n's `published in Reshumot`

-- src:ordinance:71 | ”מנשר“ או ”אכרזה“ – מנשר או אכרזה שניתנו מאת הממשלה או על פיה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "proclamation" (src:ordinance:71)
GIVEN p IS A `A proclamation or manifesto`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "proclamation" — the proclamation or manifesto is within the term:` p MEANS
       p's `given by the Government`
    OR p's `given under the Government's authority`

-- src:ordinance:78 | ”נקבע“ – נקבע בחוק שבו מצויה מלה זו או בתקנות שניתנו לפיו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "determined" (src:ordinance:78)
-- "Determined in the law in which the word appears, or in regulations given under it." The entry names a law and the regulations
-- made under that law; a regulation that itself contains the word is neither, so the entry does not say whether a determination in
-- that regulation counts, and the module refuses. `somewhere else` is another place altogether, outside the entry.
GIVEN where IS A `Where something was determined under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "determined" — it was determined, being determined` where MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `in the law in which the word appears`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in regulations made under that law`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in the regulation in which the word appears` THEN `the Ordinance's entry on "determined" says nothing of a regulation that itself uses the word`
    WHEN `somewhere else`                          THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:79 | ”עבור“ או ”הפר“, לענין דרישה או תנאי שנקבעו בחיקוק, או בכל היתר, רשיון או הרשאה אחרת, שניתנו לפי חיקוק – אף אי־קיום במשמע;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "contravene" (src:ordinance:79)
-- To contravene or breach a requirement or condition set in an enactment, or in any permit, licence or other authorisation given
-- under an enactment, includes failing to fulfil it. The conduct is asked of the Law's entry "breach", which has the same shape.
GIVEN r IS A `A requirement or condition`
      conduct IS A `Conduct towards a requirement or direction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "contravene" — the requirement or condition being` r `, the conduct being` conduct MEANS
        (   CONSIDER r
            WHEN `one set in an enactment`                                                              THEN TRUE
            WHEN `one set in a permit, licence or other authorisation given under an enactment`         THEN TRUE
            WHEN `one set in a permit given under an enactment`                                         THEN TRUE
            WHEN `one set in a licence given under an enactment`                                        THEN TRUE
            WHEN `one set in another authorisation given under an enactment`                            THEN TRUE
            WHEN `one set anywhere else`                                                                THEN FALSE)
    AND `s 3 "breach" — the conduct is a breach, the thing being a requirement or direction:` TRUE `, the conduct being` conduct

-- src:ordinance:80 | ”עבירה“ – מעשה, נסיון או מחדל, שדינם ענישה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "offence" (src:ordinance:80)
GIVEN d IS A `A deed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "offence" — the deed is an offence:` d MEANS
        (d's `an act` OR d's `an attempt` OR d's `an omission`)
    AND d's `the law on it is punishment`

-- src:ordinance:84 | ”עונש“, לענין עבירה – קנס, מאסר או כל ענישה אחרת;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "penalty" (src:ordinance:84)
GIVEN c IS A `A consequence of an offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "penalty" — the consequence is a penalty:` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a fine`                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other punishment`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not punishment`        THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:85 | ”פרק“ – פרק של החיקוק שבו מצויה מלה זו; הוא הדין לגבי ”חלק“ ”סימן“ ”סעיף“ ו”תוספת“, הכל לפי הענין;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "chapter" (src:ordinance:85)
-- "Chapter" is a chapter of the enactment in which the word stands; likewise "part", "sub-part", "section" and "schedule", as the case may be.
GIVEN x IS A `A division referred to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "chapter" — the reference is to a division of the enactment in which the word appears:` x MEANS
        x's `of the enactment in which the word appears`
    AND CONSIDER x's `the word used`
        WHEN `chapter`          THEN TRUE
        WHEN `part`             THEN TRUE
        WHEN `sub-part`         THEN TRUE
        WHEN `section`          THEN TRUE
        WHEN `schedule`         THEN TRUE
        WHEN `some other word`  THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:86 | ”סעיף קטן“ – סעיף קטן של הסעיף בו מצויה מלה זו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "subsection" (src:ordinance:86)
GIVEN x IS A `A subsection referred to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "subsection" — the reference is to a subsection of the section in which the word appears:` x MEANS
        x's `a subsection`
    AND x's `of the section in which the word appears`

-- src:ordinance:91 | ”צוואה“ – לרבות סמפון צוואה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "will" (src:ordinance:91)
-- "Includes a codicil to a will": an OPEN entry, so a document it does not list refuses unless the caller says whether it is a will
-- in the ordinary sense.
GIVEN d IS A `A testamentary document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "will" — the document is a will:` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `a will`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a codicil to a will`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not a will in its ordinary sense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else`             THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- src:ordinance:92 | ”צוות“ –
-- src:ordinance:93 | (1) לענין כלי שיט – קברניט, חובל, נווט, מכונאי, מסיק, עובד הסיפון וכל העוסק בהשטת כלי השיט וכל המשרתו;
-- src:ordinance:94 | (2) לענין כלי טיס – מפקד, טייס, נווט, מהנדס טיס וכל העוסק בהטסת כלי הטיס וכל המשרתו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "crew" (stem and limbs (1) and (2)) (src:ordinance:92-94)
-- (1) for a vessel: master, officer, navigator, mechanic, stoker, deck hand, whoever is engaged in sailing the vessel and whoever
-- serves it; (2) for an aircraft: commander, pilot, navigator, flight engineer, whoever is engaged in flying it and whoever serves it.
GIVEN craft IS A `A craft`
      role IS A `A role aboard`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "crew" — the craft being` craft `, the role is crew:` role MEANS
    CONSIDER craft
    WHEN `a vessel` THEN
        CONSIDER role
        WHEN `the master`                                      THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an officer of the ship`                          THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a navigator`                                     THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an engineer or mechanic`                         THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a stoker`                                        THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a deck hand`                                     THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anyone engaged in sailing or flying the craft`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anyone serving the craft`                        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `an aircraft` THEN
        CONSIDER role
        WHEN `the commander`                                   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a pilot`                                         THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a navigator`                                     THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a flight engineer`                               THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anyone engaged in sailing or flying the craft`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anyone serving the craft`                        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:ordinance:100 | ”רשום“, לענין מסמך – רשום לפי הדין החל על רישום אותו מסמך;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "registered" (src:ordinance:100)
GIVEN d IS A `A document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "registered" — the document is registered:` d MEANS
        d's `registered`
    AND d's `under the law that applies to the registration of that document`

-- src:ordinance:106 | ”שכירות“ – לרבות שכירות משנה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "lease" (src:ordinance:106)
-- "Includes a sublease": an OPEN entry, so a letting it does not list refuses unless the caller says whether it is a lease in the
-- ordinary sense.
GIVEN l IS A `A letting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "lease" — the letting is a lease:` l MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `a lease`          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sublease`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not a lease in its ordinary sense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else`    THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- src:ordinance:114 | ”תקנות סדרי הדין“, לענין כל בית משפט – כללים לנוהג ולסדרי הדין באותו בית משפט, שנקבעו על ידי רשות המוסמכת אותה שעה להתקין תקנות או ליתן צווים.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "rules of procedure" (src:ordinance:114)
GIVEN r IS A `A set of rules`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "rules of procedure" — the rules are the court's rules of procedure:` r MEANS
        r's `rules for the practice and procedure of the court`
    AND r's `made by an authority empowered at that time to make regulations or give orders`

-- src:ordinance:69 | ”מֶכֶר“ – לרבות חליפין, מַיִר, הצעה למכירה או הצגה למכירה;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "sale" (src:ordinance:69)
-- "Includes exchange, mayir (an exchange of goods), an offer for sale and a display for sale." Everything that is a sale in the
-- ordinary sense stays a sale. An OPEN entry: a transaction it does not list refuses unless the caller says whether it is a sale
-- in the ordinary sense.
GIVEN t IS A `A transaction or offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "sale" — the transaction or offer is a sale:` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a sale in the ordinary sense`          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an exchange`                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a mayir (an exchange of goods)`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offer for sale`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a display for sale`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not a sale in its ordinary sense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else`                         THEN `the Ordinance's entry lists what the term includes and says nothing of this unlisted thing`

-- src:ordinance:70 | ”מנדט“ – המנדט על ארץ־ישראל שמועצת חבר הלאומים אישרה אותו והגדירה תנאיו ביום עשרים וארבעה ביולי 1922;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "Mandate" (src:ordinance:70)
-- The Mandate over Palestine that the Council of the League of Nations approved and whose terms it defined on 24 July 1922.
GIVEN m IS A `A mandate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "Mandate" — the mandate is the Mandate:` m MEANS
        m's `over Palestine`
    AND m's `approved by the Council of the League of Nations and its terms defined by that Council`
    AND NOT (m's `on the day` BELOW YMD 1922 7 24)
    AND NOT (m's `on the day` ABOVE YMD 1922 7 24)

-- src:ordinance:72 | ”מסירה לדין“ – החלטה להעמיד לדין על פי כתב אישום;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "committal for trial" (src:ordinance:72)
GIVEN d IS A `A decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "committal for trial" — the decision is a committal for trial:` d MEANS
        d's `a decision to put a person on trial`
    AND d's `on the strength of an indictment`

-- src:ordinance:110 | ”תחילה“, לענין חיקוק – זמן תחילת תקפו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "commencement" (src:ordinance:110)
GIVEN t IS A `A time in the life of an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "commencement" — the time is the commencement of the enactment:` t MEANS
    t's `the time its validity begins`

-- With s 21 of the Law: an enactment's validity begins at 00:01 on its commencement day, so that moment is its commencement.
-- src:ordinance:110 | ”תחילה“, לענין חיקוק – זמן תחילת תקפו;
-- src:124 | שעת תחילת תקפו של חיקוק היא בשעה 00.01 של יום תחילתו.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "commencement" (src:ordinance:110); Interpretation Law s 21 (src:124)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Moment
`Ordinance s 1 "commencement" — by s 21 of the Law, the commencement of an enactment whose commencement day is` d MEANS
    `s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` d

-- src:ordinance:107 | ”שנה“ ו”חודש“ – למנין הלוח הגריגוריאני;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "year" and "month" (src:ordinance:107)
-- "By the Gregorian calendar", with no Hebrew-calendar clause (il-interpretation-law.l4 selects this calendar for earlier enactments).
GIVETH A Calendar
`Ordinance s 1 "year" and "month" — the calendar the Ordinance gives` MEANS
    `the Gregorian calendar`

§§ `Entries about property`

-- src:ordinance:65 | ”מיטלטלין“ או ”טובין“ – נכסים מוחשיים, חוץ ממקרקעין; אולם מקום שהמלה ”מיטלטלין“ או ”טובין“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:65 | חוק המיטלטלין, תשל״א–1971, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אילולא
-- src:ordinance:65 | החוק האמור;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "movables" (src:ordinance:65)
-- "Tangible property, except immovables": the same words as s 3 of the Law, so this calls the Law's function.
GIVEN t IS A `A thing of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "movables" — the thing is movable, as the Ordinance now defines it:` t MEANS
    `s 3 "movables" — the thing is movable:` t

-- src:ordinance:66 | ההגדרה החלה על חיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:66 | חוק המיטלטלין, תשל״א–1971: ”מיטלטלין“ או ”טובין“ – כל נכס למינהו, חוץ ממקרקעין;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "movables", the note: the earlier meaning (src:ordinance:66)
-- "Any property of any kind, except immovables." Whether the property is immovable is a fact the caller supplies, because in
-- an enactment that old the word "immovables" has its own earlier meaning.
GIVEN p IS A `A piece of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "movables" — in an enactment given before the Movables Law, the thing is within the earlier meaning:` p MEANS
        p's `property of any kind`
    AND NOT p's `immovable`

-- src:ordinance:75 | ”מקרקעין“ – קרקע, כל הבנוי והנטוע עליה וכל דבר אחר המחובר אליה חיבור של קבע, זולת מחוברים הניתנים להפרדה; אולם מקום שהמלה ”מקרקעין“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:75 | חוק המקרקעין, תשכ״ט–1969, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא
-- src:ordinance:75 | החוק האמור;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "immovables" (src:ordinance:75)
-- Land, everything built and planted on it, and anything else attached to it permanently, except detachable fixtures:
-- the same words as s 3 of the Law, so this calls the Law's function and takes the same reading (fork F27).
GIVEN t IS A `A thing of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "immovables" — the thing is immovable, as the Ordinance now defines it:` t MEANS
    `s 3 "immovables" — the thing is immovable:` t

@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "immovables" (the other reading of the exception, F27) (src:ordinance:75)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "immovables" — the thing is immovable, if the exception for detachable fixtures reaches every limb:` t MEANS
    `s 3 "immovables" — the thing is immovable, if the exception for detachable fixtures reaches every limb:` t

-- src:ordinance:76 | ההגדרה החלה על חיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:76 | חוק המקרקעין, תשכ״ט–1969: ”מקרקעין“ – קרקע מכל סוג ומכל צורת החזקה, וכל בנין, עץ או דבר אחר המחובר לקרקע, וכל חלק של ים, של חוף או של נהר, וכל זכות, טובת הנאה או שעבוד הנאה בקרקע או במים או מעליהם;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "immovables", the note: the earlier meaning (src:ordinance:76)
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate for the earlier meaning of immovables`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "immovables" — in an enactment given before the Land Law, the candidate is within the earlier meaning:` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `land of every kind and every form of holding`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a building, tree or other thing attached to land`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a building attached to land`                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a tree attached to land`                                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another thing attached to land`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a part of the sea, the shore or a river`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a part of the sea`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a part of the shore`                                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a part of a river`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a right, benefit or easement in land or in or over water`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a right in land or in or over water`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a benefit in land or in or over water`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an easement in land or in or over water`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anything else`                                                  THEN FALSE

-- src:ordinance:111 | ”תפישה“, לענין מקרקעין – לרבות השימוש, הדירה, ההחזקה או ההנאה שלא כעובד וכפקיד בלבד ולשם השגחה או שמירה בלבד;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "possession" (src:ordinance:111)
-- "Includes use, residence, possession or enjoyment not merely as an employee and official and not merely for supervision
-- and guarding." READING TAKEN (fork F28, the same question as in s 3 of the Law): neither exclusion may hold. The Ordinance joins
-- the exclusions with "and" where the Law has "or"; the Ordinance lists "residence" where the Law does not.
GIVEN h IS A `A holding of land under the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "possession" — the holding of land is possession:` h MEANS
       h's `possession in the ordinary sense`
    OR (    (   h's `use, residence, possession or enjoyment`
             OR h's `use`
             OR h's `residence`
             OR h's `possession`
             OR h's `enjoyment`)
        AND NOT h's `as an employee or official only`
        AND NOT h's `for supervision or guarding only`)

-- src:ordinance:68 | לפי
-- src:ordinance:68 | סעיף 1(ב) לחוק מימי חופין, תשי״ז–1956, ההגדרה שלהלן תחול גם על חיקוקים והוראות מינהל שניתנו לפני תחילתו של
-- src:ordinance:68 | חוק הפרשנות: ”מימי חופין“ – רצועת ים פתוח לאורך חופי המדינה, ברוחב שנים עשר מילים מנקודת שפל המים שבחוף;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "coastal waters", the note: the strip (src:ordinance:68)
-- The entry reads "(בוטלה)" and its note gives the strip as an open sea along the coast of the State, twelve "miles" wide from the
-- low-water point on the shore. s 3 of the Law gives twelve NAUTICAL miles, and the Law's note says the definition reaches earlier
-- enactments too. READING TAKEN (fork F29): both texts name one strip, so the note's strip is the Law's, in nautical miles.
GIVEN p IS A `A point at sea`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "coastal waters" — the note's strip, read as the Law's twelve nautical miles:` p MEANS
    `s 3 "coastal waters" — the point is within the coastal waters:` p

-- The other reading (F29): the note's "miles" are statute miles. The conversion (a nautical mile is 1852 metres, a statute mile
-- 1609.344 metres) is not in the sources; it is the one fact from outside them that this reading needs.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "coastal waters", the note read literally in statute miles (src:ordinance:68)
GIVEN p IS A `A point at sea`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 "coastal waters" — the note's strip, read literally as twelve statute miles:` p MEANS
        p's `it is in the open sea along the coast of the State`
    AND p's `its distance seaward from the low-water point on the shore, in nautical miles` AT LEAST 0
    AND (p's `its distance seaward from the low-water point on the shore, in nautical miles` TIMES 1852) AT MOST (12 TIMES 1609.344)

§§ `The dispatcher: which meaning governs a word, and which enactments the Ordinance's definitions govern`

-- src:ordinance:48 | ”חוק“ – דבר חקיקה של הכנסת ולרבות כל פקודה; אולם מקום שהמלה ”חוק“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני פרסום הנוסח החדש לפקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא הנוסח החדש;
-- src:ordinance:52 | ”חיקוק“ – כל חוק וכל תקנה בין שניתנו לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו ובין שניתנו לאחריה; אולם מקום שהמלה ”חיקוק“ באה בפקודה או בתקנה שניתנו לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא פקודה זו;
-- src:ordinance:65 | ”מיטלטלין“ או ”טובין“ – נכסים מוחשיים, חוץ ממקרקעין; אולם מקום שהמלה ”מיטלטלין“ או ”טובין“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:65 | חוק המיטלטלין, תשל״א–1971, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אילולא
-- src:ordinance:65 | החוק האמור;
-- src:ordinance:75 | ”מקרקעין“ – קרקע, כל הבנוי והנטוע עליה וכל דבר אחר המחובר אליה חיבור של קבע, זולת מחוברים הניתנים להפרדה; אולם מקום שהמלה ”מקרקעין“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:75 | חוק המקרקעין, תשכ״ט–1969, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא
-- src:ordinance:75 | החוק האמור;
-- src:ordinance:87 | ”פקודה“ – כל פקודה שניתנה מאת מועצת המדינה הזמנית וכל פקודה שניתנה כדין בארץ ישראל לפני הקמת המדינה, ופקודה זו בכלל; אולם מקום שהמלה ”פקודה“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא פקודה זו;
-- src:ordinance:112 | ”תקנה“ – תקנה, כלל, חוק עזר, מנשר, אכרזה, צו, הוראה, הודעה, מודעה, או מסמך אחר, שניתנו מאת כל רשות בארץ ישראל או בישראל, בין לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו ובין לאחריה, מכוח חוק, או מכוח אקט של הפרלמנט הבריטי או מכוח דבר־המלך־במועצה, לרבות צו, הוראה, הודעה, מודעה או מסמך אחר שניתנו על יסוד תקנה, כלל או חוק עזר כאמור; אולם מקום שהמלה ”תקנה“ באה בחיקוק שניתן לפני תחילת תקפה של פקודה זו, תהא משמעותה כמשמעות שהיתה נודעת לה אלמלא פקודה זו;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1, the provisos of "statute" (src:ordinance:48); "enactment" (src:ordinance:52); "movables" (src:ordinance:65); "immovables" (src:ordinance:75); "ordinance" (src:ordinance:87); "regulation" (src:ordinance:112)
GIVEN w IS A `A word with an earlier meaning`
      age IS AN `The age of the enactment a word stands in`
GIVETH A `Which meaning of a word governs`
`Ordinance s 1 — which meaning governs the word` w `in an enactment of the age` age MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `the word statute` THEN
        IF age's `given before the new text of the Ordinance was published`
        THEN `the earlier meaning that the Ordinance's note states`
        ELSE `the definition the Ordinance now states`
    WHEN `the word enactment` THEN
        IF age's `given before the Ordinance began to have effect`
        THEN `the earlier meaning, which this text does not state`
        ELSE `the definition the Ordinance now states`
    WHEN `the word ordinance` THEN
        IF age's `given before the Ordinance began to have effect`
        THEN `the earlier meaning that the Ordinance's note states`
        ELSE `the definition the Ordinance now states`
    WHEN `the word regulation` THEN
        IF age's `given before the Ordinance began to have effect`
        THEN `the earlier meaning that the Ordinance's note states`
        ELSE `the definition the Ordinance now states`
    WHEN `the word movables` THEN
        IF age's `given before the Movables Law, 5731-1971, began to have effect`
        THEN `the earlier meaning that the Ordinance's note states`
        ELSE `the definition the Ordinance now states`
    WHEN `the word immovables` THEN
        IF age's `given before the Land Law, 5729-1969, began to have effect`
        THEN `the earlier meaning that the Ordinance's note states`
        ELSE `the definition the Ordinance now states`

-- src:ordinance:12 | פקודת הפרשנות בוטלה והוחלפה ברובה על ידי
-- src:ordinance:12 | חוק הפרשנות, התשמ״א–1981 (להלן – חוק הפרשנות); לפי
-- src:ordinance:12 | סעיפים 1
-- src:ordinance:12 | ו־3 לחוק הפרשנות
-- src:ordinance:12 | וסעיף 1(ב) לחוק מימי חופין, תשי״ז–1956,
-- src:ordinance:12 | חוק הפרשנות יחול לגבי כל חיקוק והוראת מינהל, אף אם ניתנו לפני תחילתו, אם אין הוראה אחרת לענין הנדון ואם אין בענין הנדון או בהקשרו דבר שאינו מתיישב עם
-- src:ordinance:12 | חוק הפרשנות; אולם על מלים וביטויים – למעט ”חטא“, ”עוון“, ”פשע“, ”מימי חופין“ ו”שנת כספים“ – שבחיקוקים והוראות מינהל שניתנו לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:12 | חוק הפרשנות (ביום 1 באוקטובר 1981) לא יחול
-- src:ordinance:12 | סעיף 3 לחוק אלא יוסיפו לחול ההגדרות
-- src:ordinance:12 | שבסעיף 1 לפקודת הפרשנות.
