@ref Interpretation Ordinance, the note at its head (src:ordinance:12); s 1, its note and opening words (src:ordinance:31-32); the five repealed entries and their notes: "sin" (src:ordinance:50-51), "coastal waters" (src:ordinance:67-68), "misdemeanour" (src:ordinance:82-83), "felony" (src:ordinance:89-90), "fiscal year" (src:ordinance:108-109); Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22)
GIVEN entry IS AN `An entry of Ordinance section 1`
      m IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance's definitions govern` entry `in an enactment given at` m MEANS
    CONSIDER entry
    WHEN `the Ordinance entry on "sin"`            THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Ordinance entry on "misdemeanour"`   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Ordinance entry on "felony"`         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Ordinance entry on "coastal waters"` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Ordinance entry on "fiscal year"`    THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given at` m
-- src:ordinance:31 | בהתאם
-- src:ordinance:31 | לסעיפים 1
-- src:ordinance:31 | ו־3 לחוק הפרשנות
-- src:ordinance:31 | וסעיף 1(ב) לחוק מימי חופין, תשי״ז–1956, ההגדרות להלן חלות על מלים וביטויים – למעט ”חטא“, ”עוון“, ”פשע“, ”שנת כספים“, ו”מימי חופין“ – שבחיקוקים ובהוראות מינהל שניתנו לפני תחילת
-- src:ordinance:31 | חוק הפרשנות.
-- src:ordinance:32 | בפקודה זו, ובכל חיקוק שהוא בר־תוקף כיום, ובכל חיקוק שיינתן מכאן ואילך, יתפרשו כל מלה וניב שבסעיף זה כאמור בצדם להלן:
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1, its note and opening words (the kinds of instrument its definitions reach) (src:ordinance:31-32)
-- The note says the definitions apply to the words of enactments AND of administrative directions given before the Law; the opening words
-- speak of enactments. A private contract and any other document are named nowhere, so the definitions do not reach them (FALSE:
-- "not reached", not "the Ordinance says no"). For an enactment or an administrative direction the answer is the dispatcher's, by date.
GIVEN entry IS AN `An entry of Ordinance section 1`
      kind IS A `A kind of instrument`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance's definitions govern` entry `in an instrument of the kind` kind `given on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the instrument is an enactment`                THEN `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance's definitions govern` entry `in an enactment given on` d
    WHEN `the instrument is an administrative direction` THEN `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance's definitions govern` entry `in an enactment given on` d
    WHEN `the instrument is a private contract`          THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the instrument is some other document`         THEN FALSE

